{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0181Vto7ifxPPWRXVpdXXWpk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies output parity through differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go implementations), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (Darwin/Linux syscall abstraction), `pkg/format/` (shared output formatting), `magefiles/` (build targets, excluded from generation).\n\n**Current State:** Source code exists for `pkg/format/` (color.go, size.go, table.go), `pkg/sys/` (stat.go, stat_darwin.go, stat_linux.go, terminal.go), and `pkg/testutils/` (difftest.go). No test files exist for any of these packages. No `cmd/` implementations exist on the working branch.\n\n**Current Release (00.0):** \"Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure\" with four use cases:\n- uc001-magefiles — excluded from generation scope (DD7)\n- uc002-format — implementation exists, **tests missing**\n- uc003-sys — implementation exists, **tests missing**\n- uc004-testutils — implementation exists, **tests missing**\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nAll three generatable use cases in rel00.0 have implementations but no tests. By canonical ordering (alphabetical on file path when otherwise equal), `pkg/format/` tests come first. The format package is self-contained (no external binary or platform dependencies for testing), making it the lowest-risk starting point.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd003-format R1, R2, R3 -- unit tests for pkg/format/\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd003-format.yaml (requirement definitions for R1, R2, R3)\n      - pkg/format/table.go (Columns, PadRight, PadLeft, displayWidth implementations)\n      - pkg/format/color.go (FileTypeColor, Reset, ColorEnabled, SetColorEnabled, ResetColorEnabled implementations)\n      - pkg/format/size.go (HumanSize, HumanSizeOpts implementations)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/table_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Tests for Columns, PadRight, PadLeft, displayWidth\n      - path: pkg/format/color_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Tests for FileTypeColor, Reset, ColorEnabled, SetColorEnabled, ResetColorEnabled\n      - path: pkg/format/size_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Tests for HumanSize with binary and SI modes\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test table formatting functions per prd003-format R1: Columns produces correct row-major grid for various entry counts and terminal widths (R1.1, R1.4), PadRight and PadLeft pad to exact display width (R1.2), displayWidth counts runes not bytes (R1.3)\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test ANSI color functions per prd003-format R2: FileTypeColor returns correct escape sequence for each file type -- directory, symlink, executable, block device, char device, socket, named pipe -- and empty string for regular files (R2.1, R2.4); Reset returns ANSI reset when color is active and empty string when disabled (R2.2); ColorEnabled returns false for non-TTY writers (R2.3); SetColorEnabled overrides TTY detection (R2.6); ResetColorEnabled reverts to auto mode (R2.7)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test human-readable size formatting per prd003-format R3: HumanSize returns '0' for zero, plain integer below first threshold, one decimal place for values under 10 in a unit, zero decimal places otherwise; verify both binary (1024-based with K/M/G/T/P/E suffixes) and SI (1000-based with kB/MB/GB/TB suffixes) modes\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use SetColorEnabled(true) and SetColorEnabled(false) per prd003-format R2.6 to force color state in tests without requiring a real TTY. Call ResetColorEnabled() in deferred cleanup per prd003-format R2.7 to avoid leaking state between tests.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Test Columns with row-major (across) order per prd003-format R1.4. Verify entries fill rows left-to-right, not columns top-to-bottom.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./pkg/format/... passes with no failures\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"table_test.go covers Columns with 0 entries (nil return), single entry, entries fitting multiple columns, entries requiring single-column fallback, and verifies row-major ordering\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"color_test.go covers FileTypeColor for all 7 file types (directory, symlink, executable, block device, char device, socket, named pipe) plus regular file, and verifies empty strings when color is disabled via SetColorEnabled(false)\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"size_test.go covers HumanSize for zero, sub-threshold integers, single-decimal-place values (under 10 in a unit), zero-decimal-place values (10 and above), and the highest suffix in both Binary and SI modes\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":46346,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bfc2929-6ec8-409f-a99d-934c86e11f8c","uuid":"3eba79be-1710-4eb9-a7c0-9e70f8fba2a5"}
